INSTALL
=======

Requirements
------------
- Ubuntu 18.04 or later, or any Debian-based system
- bash 4.0 or higher (pre-installed on all modern Ubuntu/Debian)
- no other dependencies

Installing from the .deb package
---------------------------------
Download the latest .deb from the releases page and run:

    sudo dpkg -i elite-roast_1.0_all.deb

Open a new terminal. Roasting starts immediately.

Building from source
--------------------
    git clone https://github.com/Nishanthc08/elite-roast.git
    cd elite-roast
    bash build.sh
    sudo dpkg -i elite-roast_1.0_all.deb

Removing
--------
    sudo apt remove elite-roast

This removes all installed files and cleans up .bashrc for all users.

Verifying removal
-----------------
After removal, all of these should return nothing:

    dpkg -l | grep elite-roast
    ls /etc/profile.d/ | grep roast
    grep roast ~/.bashrc
    which roast-stats
